.TH FERMINAL 1 "August 2026" "Ferminal 1.4.3" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
ferminal \- lightweight terminal wrapper

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B <ferminal-command> | <value>
.RI 

.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferminal is a lightweight, Python-based interactive shell wrapper that provides short aliases for common filesystem, Git, and installation tasks.
It is designed to reduce typing and improve workflow speed by using single-letter commands for frequently used operations.

.PP
Note: Ferminal behaves as an interactive shell. Run
.B ferminal
and then enter commands at the prompt.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display usage information and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
The following commands are available inside the Ferminal shell.
.TP
.B h
Show the built-in help menu.

.TP
.B x
Exit the Ferminal shell.

.TP
.B b
Clear the screen.

.TP
.B l
List directory contents.

.TP
.B la
List all files including hidden entries.

.TP
.B w
Show the current working directory.

.TP
.B d <path>
Change the current directory to <path>.

.TP
.B k <name>
Create a new directory named <name>.

.TP
.B f <name>
Create a new file named <name>.

.TP
.B m <name>
Remove the directory named <name>.

.TP
.B n <name>
Remove the file named <name>.

.TP
.B v <source> <destination>
Move a file or directory.

.TP
.B c <source> <destination>
Copy a file.

.TP
.B cr <source> <destination>
Copy a directory recursively.

.TP
.B u <file>
Show the contents of <file>.

.TP
.B e <text>
Print <text> to the terminal.

.TP
.B z
Pause for thirty seconds.

.TP
.B p <host>
Run ping against <host>.

.SH COMMANDS \( Project Generator\)
Check or update the project template repository, then generate a project from the selected template.
Supported templates: py, blog, doc, love2d, react.
.TP
.B nm py
Generate Python app.

.TP
.B nm blog
Generate Blog template.

.TP
.B doc
Generate Documentation template.

.TP
.B love2d
Generate love2d template.

.TP
.B react
Generate react template.

.SH COMMANDS \( GIT\)
The following Git aliases are available inside the Ferminal shell.
.TP
.B gia <path>
Stage changes for <path>.

.TP
.B gis
Show Git status.

.TP
.B gic <repository>
Clone a Git repository.

.TP
.B gin
Initialize a Git repository.

.TP
.B gib <branch>
Create a new branch named <branch>.

.TP
.B gibd <branch>
Delete the branch named <branch>.

.TP
.B gip
Pull updates from a remote repository.

.TP
.B gih
Push commits to a remote repository.

.TP
.B gim <message>
Commit staged changes with message <message>.

.TP
.B gil
Show the Git log.

.TP
.B gif <remote>
Fetch updates from <remote>.

.TP
.B gir <args>
Manage Git remotes.

.TP
.B gie <branch>
Merge <branch> into the current branch.

.TP
.B gio <branch>
Check out <branch>.

.TP
.B giob <branch>
Create and switch to a new branch named <branch>.

.TP
.B gig <tag>
Create a Git tag named <tag>.

.TP
.B gid <path>
Show changes for <path>.

.TP
.B girh
Reset the current index (HEAD).

.TP
.B girs <path>
Restore <path> from the working tree.

.TP
.B gist
Stash changes.

.TP
.B gista
Apply the latest stash.

.TP
.B gifd
Clean untracked files and directories.

.TP
.B gish <object>
Show Git object details.

.TP
.B gibl <file>
Show blame information for <file>.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ferminal
Start the Ferminal interactive shell.

.TP
.B h
Show the help menu inside Ferminal.

.TP
.B d C:\\Users\\Example
Change to the specified directory.

.TP
.B k project
Create a directory named project.

.TP
.B gim "Initial commit"
Commit changes with a message.

